{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #346: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $A=\\{1\\leq a_1< a_2<\\cdots\\}$ be a set of integers such that\n{UL}\n{LI} $A\\backslash B$ is complete for any finite subset $B$ and {/LI}\n{LI} $A\\backslash B$ is not complete for any infinite subset $B$.{/LI}\n{/UL}\n(Here 'complete' means all sufficiently large integers can be written as a sum of distinct members of the sequence.)\n\nIs it true that if $a_{n+1}/a_n \\geq 1+\\epsilon$ for some $\\epsilon>0$ and all $n$ then\\[\\lim_n \\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{2}?\\] Prize: no. Tags: complete sequences, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_c991ca71cdf2d5ee79efab968002aa283cf86a4cfdee4a4e8db1558e4a62fa9c","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:346","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_d0075ee0b708f87c","object_root":"sha256:5568d10488dd50dfa2e1e75b26bb6b2d1a43c3fcd6fe86886b3ef788ac446ec8","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title"